    "original_review_scope_verbatim": "Complete original Proposition 5.1, with all critical-point/stratum/tangent-cone definitions and full author cell-construction proof. Retains the actual minima/filling/balanced-locus geometry and gradient/triangulation context needed for the local argument, plus eight unchanged original explanatory figures. A narrow typography-only resolver renders the verified blackboard-bold letter arguments of mathbbm using AMS mathbb: N, Z, Q, R, P, C, K, W and D; there are no numeric/indicator/general-expression calls in this source. Literal author body commands and mathematics are unchanged. The later illustration subsection and boundary-point sequel are excluded.\n\nNo mathematical refereeing or assistant-generated proof. Native source and corresponding saved publisher PDF are hash-bound. Fresh two-pass XeLaTeX with existing cache and -no-shell-escape passed. Final log has no undefined references/citations, missing glyphs, or overfull boxes. The full Proposition5.1 statement, codimension/tangent-space conditions, original Figure8, balanced simplices and final filling/closedness step were compared with publisher PDF pages27–28 and rendered pages23–24. Blackboard-bold field/set letter uses were compared in the definition context; AMS glyphs differ only typographically and retain the verified same field/set role. Introduction189,199–210 explicitly positions this as one of the paper’s three outcomes (Proposition1.3 restated as5.1), not an adjacent technical lemma.\n",
